{"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"OpenUSD"}],"title":"Working with TfNotice"},"abstract":[{"text":"Learn how to use the TfNotice notification subsystem in Swift","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD"]]},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenUSD includes a notification subsystem based on "},{"code":"pxr::TfNotice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"pxr::TfNotice::Register","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" for use in C++. SwiftUsd exposes this system to Swift with minor modifications."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Like in C++, TfNotice registration in Swift comes in three main forms:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:)"}],"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:)","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:)-28red"},{"type":"text","text":" to register for a particular notice type, regardless of sender"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:_:)-22ec6","isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:_:)","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr.TfNotice.Register(_:_:_:)"}]},{"text":" to register for a particular notice type from a specific sender, without retrieving the sender in the notification callback","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/OpenUSD\/C++\/pxr\/TfNotice\/Register(_:_:_:)-21npb","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pxr.TfNo